From 3f205a7cd8f11a5fe78596837e57c447d9c259e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AppDrop iOS3 fix <appdrop@zo.computer>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 16:45:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?ios3:=20blocks=20aren't=20ObjC=20objects=20on?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=203.1=20=E2=80=94=20back=20copy-block=20properties=20with=20C?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20blocks=20runtime=20+=20NSBlockOperation=20backport?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Second crash was EXC_BAD_ACCESS/SIGBUS at 0x0 in objc_msgSend, from
-[CategoryTileView setOnTap:] (the synthesized @property(copy) setter ->
objc_setProperty -> -copyWithZone:) while buildContent assigned each tile's
onTap after the catalog loaded. On iOS 3.1 NSBlock doesn't exist: a block's
isa points at the all-zero _NSConcrete*Block storage, so sending a block ANY
ObjC message (-copyWithZone:/-copy/collection -retain) dereferences garbage.

Fix (systemic, not per-screen):
- AppDropBlocks.{h,m}: AD_BLOCK_ACCESSORS macro (manual copy-property block
  accessors via _Block_copy/_Block_release, never messaging a block) + ADBlockBox
  to store blocks in NSArray/NSDictionary.
- Convert all 8 copy-block properties across 5 classes (CategoryTileView onTap/
  onDelete, AppTileView onTap, AppRowCell onTileTap/isAppSelectedBlock,
  FilePicker onPick, UpdateNotes installHandler) to @dynamic + the macro.
- Replace explicit [block copy] sends (CategoryTileView -tapped, AppTileView
  -tapped, UpdateNotes -installTapped) with the heap-stored ivar.
- IconLoader: box completion blocks with ADBlockBox before storing in the
  pending-waiters arrays; unbox in fireWaiters.
- AppDropBlockOp.m + compat decl: ADBlockOperation (NSOperation subclass)
  backports NSBlockOperation (iOS 4.0+), macro-rewritten so IconLoader's
  network-fetch path doesn't throw on the first uncached icon.
